        "origin": "canon",
        "lore": "Prototype designation for the Type-00, built in the same four Royal Guard variants (XR, XF, XA, XC). During the 1998 Defense of Kyoto, at Takatsukasa Kyoko's request and on the Shogun's orders, one of each variant was pulled from transfer to the rear and sortied to rescue 2nd Lieutenants Takamura Yui, Yamashiro Kazusa and Noto Izumi. Kyoko, piloting the Type-98XR, located Yui and cleared a swarm of Tank-class BETA with only a Type-74 PB Blade and a Type-87 Assault Cannon. The sortie proved the design's melee and close-range capability, and news of it lifted morale among hard-pressed Japanese troops.",
        "attribution": "wiki",
        "publishStatus": "published"
      }
